!! Source

''This carrier names an AGGREGATE, never a file.'' `bootTrustedModules` holds its address as `MODULE_AGGREGATE_URI`; after at least one gated module injects, the gate reads this tiddler's text and hands it to `tw.modules.define(moduleText, "library", "lararium-tw5-modules")` — one call, one library name, whatever body stands here at boot.

An empty body defines an empty library, which the gate treats as a no-op. The `tw5-module-name` field carries the library name TW5 registers it under.

The sigil declarations and render templates that make up the wikitext surface travel a different road: `scripts/build-plugin-tiddler.ts` folds `packages/lararium-tw5/tiddlers/*.tid` into `src/plugin-tiddler.generated.ts`, and the plugin ships them as shadow tiddlers. No gate stands in that path — a shadow tiddler carries no executable body.

